# Secrets — the n8n API key lives here and must never be committed.
.env
.env.local

# Disposable caches. The n8n cache holds error messages pulled from live
# executions; keep it out of history for the same reason as .env.
.cache-scan.json
.cache-n8n-exec.json
scan.json

# Claude fix runs. Each one holds the RAW workflow (credential ids, node
# parameters with session keys) plus the pre-apply backup. Local scratch, never
# committed — proposals.json carries the part worth keeping.
.claude-runs/

# Tester (PLAN.md). The catalog holds only sanitized parameter SHAPES, but it is
# regenerable in one command, so it is a cache. The run dirs are scratch. The
# docs cache is third-party web text with a TTL — deliberately NOT tracked
# knowledge, so a poisoned or stale fetch can never become permanent.
.cache-catalog.json
.cache-catalog.json.tmp
.tester-runs/
.cache-tester-docs/
# Rascunho da rodada diária das novidades. O que sobrevive dela é o
# `n8n-novidades.md` e o `novidades.json`, os dois versionados.
.novidades-run/

# The n8n node packages, unpacked from npm. 83MB of third-party code, fetched by
# `node esquema.js --baixar`, read only at extraction time — nothing in the running
# server requires anything from here, so the zero-runtime-dependency rule holds.
# Regenerable in one command, and pinned by version inside .cache-esquema.json.
.n8n-pkgs/

# The distilled node schema. A cache: derived from the packages above, keyed by
# their version, and rebuilt in one command. What makes it a cache and not
# knowledge is that npm is the source of truth and it is still there.
.cache-esquema.json
.cache-esquema.json.tmp

# Screenshots produced while iterating on the design. The preview .html files
# are kept (they are the record of what was chosen); the PNGs are regenerable.
preview/*.png
*.png

# fixes.json and proposals.json are NOT caches — they are knowledge that exists
# nowhere else and cannot be regenerated from the API, so they stay tracked.
# Only the atomic-write temp files are disposable.
fixes.json.tmp
proposals.json.tmp
# licoes.json segue a mesma regra e pelo mesmo motivo: a rodada reprovada que
# gerou uma licao nao existe mais em lugar nenhum, e a curadoria do Kauan
# (promovida / descartada) e decisao dele. Rastreado. So o temp sai.
licoes.json.tmp

# Skill instalada localmente por `npx skills add`: 19MB e 201 arquivos, com
# node_modules de terceiro dentro, num repositorio cuja regra e ter zero
# dependencia. `skills-lock.json` fica versionado — ele e o que permite
# reinstalar exatamente a mesma versao.
.agents/
.claude/skills/

# projetos/ NAO entra aqui de proposito: e o que o Tester produziu e o Kauan
# decidiu guardar. O JSON do fluxo, o relatorio e a simulacao nao se regeneram
# sem pagar a construcao de novo.
